    fix(frontend): give every read a deadline, and let an answered origin speak for itself (ORD-0263)
    
    A silent origin used to be unclassifiable because it was never an event: `v8Request` and
    `requestJson` had no deadline, so the boot `await` never settled, its catch never ran, and the
    traveller stayed on 「正在准备城市周末行程…」 while a local snapshot sat unread in IndexedDB.
    `probeHealth()` then folded "answered 500" and "never answered" into one boolean, so the two
    remaining states could not be told apart either.
    
    - lib/readDeadline.ts: per-deadline GET/HEAD reads only, with `ReadDeadlineMissed` distinguishable
      from both a caller abort and a transport error; writes are untouched on purpose.
    - classifyHealthProbe takes four measured bits (answered/status/ok/timed_out) instead of one bool.
    - withCachedCopyFact folds the read-back of a local copy into the same classification object, so the
      snapshot sentence and the recovery door are carried by a measurement, not by a guess.
    - New failure.noAnswer copy quotes the deadline constant; the cached-copy screen's chip now follows
      the classification too (本地快照 · 只读 when the origin answered).

